    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored today by **Isaac Paredes** (72.13) and **Josh Naylor** (69.06), both of whom benefit from favorable matchups against starters with xERAs near 4.80. **Paredes** is our elite play, utilizing a significant platoon edge against Quantrill to maximize his scoring floor. Meanwhile, **Kyle Karros** (63.93) has surged into a must-start role; despite facing Ray, **Karros** benefits from a massive 19% SP skill adjustment and a favorable wind-out projection, pushing his efficiency significantly higher than his base. **Seiya Suzuki** (63.88) also rates as a strong start, though his outlook is tempered by a 35% rain risk in his contest against Greene.\n\nOur stolen base-focused strategy remains selective today given the defensive profiles of opposing catchers. **Corbin Carroll** (59.88) and **James Wood** (56.57) both face high-skill catchers, which has suppressed their base running expectations. Consequently, **Austin Riley** (57.87) is the most notable exclusion from the starting nine. While **Riley**\u2019s projection was solid, he ultimately landed on the bench because his 57.87 score couldn't overcome the efficiency gains provided by the platoon advantages and batting order stability of our chosen OF and UTIL starters. We are prioritizing the high-leverage spots of **Travis Bazzana** and **Tyler Soderstrom** to capture run production, as their path to scoring hinges more on situational hitting than the difficult-to-convert stolen base opportunities today.",
